  "description": "The proposal is to operate a small plate restaurant named \"Ebi\" on the ground floor and basement of the premises. The layout includes a fixed bar counter with stools on the ground floor and tables on the basement, but no standing area for customers. All service is to seated guests only, with no vertical drinking permitted.\r\nThe food offer includes a seasonal menu of 7–8 small plate dishes such as house-made terrine and pâté, local cheese, Japanese-style donburi bowls, and daily vegetable dishes. All food is prepared on-site using a small kitchen fitted with essential commercial equipment (e.g., undercounter fridge, induction hob, and oven).\r\nAlcohol is served strictly ancillary to food. Off-sales are limited to sealed containers only.\r\nThe maximum capacity is 20 customers. There is no takeaway or delivery service. Music will be limited to low-volume background music only.\r\nOpening hours are 12:00 to 22:30, Monday to Sunday. The rear garden closes to customers at 21:00, in line with the Premises Licence conditions.\r\nWritten advice (only)\t£942.97 \t£188.59\t£1,131.56",
